      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Scan print is broken/faint in places; cells left \"\" where the glyph could not be read with confidence. In this bold face 3/8 and 5/6 are easily confused on this scan.",
        "1866 Lowest — Feet: \"—2\" read from a damaged glyph (tail and base of 2 visible).",
        "1867 Lowest — Feet: only the top arc of a digit survives (probably 0); unreadable. 1867 Lowest — Inches: only a short vertical stroke survives; unreadable.",
        "1868 Lowest — Feet: only the lower half of the glyph printed; read as 0.",
        "1872 Highest — Inches: bold digit reads as either 3 or 8; left blank.",
        "1875 Highest — Day: \"1?th\", second digit broken (10th or 16th?); left blank.",
        "1883 Lowest — Feet: digit fragment only (possibly 2); unreadable.",
        "1887 Lowest — Feet: bold digit 3 or 8; left blank. 1887 Highest — Feet: \"†4?\" second digit damaged (6 or 8?); left blank.",
        "1889 Highest — Inches: bold digit 3 or 8; left blank.",
        "1890 Lowest — Feet: damaged glyph (possibly 0 or 5); unreadable. 1890 Lowest — Inches: bold 3 or 8; left blank.",
        "1895 Highest — Day: first digit faint (\"?4th\", probably 24th); left blank.",
        "1901 Lowest — Feet: \"—3\" or \"—8\", the dash runs into the digit; left blank.",
        "1907 Lowest — Day: \"25th\" or \"26th\", ambiguous; left blank.",
        "1920 Highest — Day: first digit broken (\"?1st\"); Feet: \"45\" or \"46\" ambiguous; Inches: blotted. All three left blank.",
        "1922 Lowest — Feet: only top arc of the digit printed; unreadable.",
        "1921, 1922, 1923, 1924 and 1926 Highest — Inches: cell is empty in print (no figure printed), not a reading failure.",
        "1910 (49 ft.) and 1926 (49 ft.) are printed without the † mark although above the stated Bund level of 46 — transcribed as printed.",
        "Date column split into Month and Day for clarity; day text kept as printed (e.g. \"21st & 22nd\", \"26th and 27th\", \"27 8th\").",
        "No totals printed."
