      "chapter": "General Information",
      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Known localities of alkaline igneous rocks in China]",
      "caption_extra": "Section: Geology. Geology—Igneous Rocks. \"Alkaline rocks:—Alkaline igneous rocks are of rather rare occurrence in China. The following localities have been known, however, through recent studies:\"",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "No.",
            "Item"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(1)",
              "Nephelite syenite at east of Hui-li, Szechwan, found by Leclère. To the W. of the district, V. K. Ting found another exposure of the same composition."
            ],
            [
              "(2)",
              "Richeckite granite near Foochow, described by Koto."
            ],
            [
              "(3)",
              "At Tze-chin-shan W. Shansi, a nephelite syenite intruded in Mesozoic beds has differentiated into a series of volcanic eruptions including leucite tinguite. This was discovered and studied by Norin."
            ],
            [
              "(4)",
              "An analcite syenite porphyry at Ling-feng-hsien, Shansi, described by L. F. Yih."
            ],
            [
              "(5)",
              "In W. Tienshan, nephelite syenite and sodalite syenite are known through Preobrajensky's study."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Numbered list of short paragraphs, single Item column."
      ],
      "continued": false,
